kunzite: Adreno 710 step 14, the GMU firmware (kgpu=14; 1-12 unchanged, 13 reworked).
13 now builds its tables with a small page-table builder (3 levels of 4K, 39-bit) whose 8 tables
come from a pool made before the context is on (freed at the end, after stream 5 is unrouted);
its test page moves to GMU 0x7ffff000, since the firmware wants 0x60000000. 14 reads
/usr/share/firmware/kunzite/gmu_gen70000.bin (uploaded once) and does what kgsl's
gen7_gmu_parse_fw / gen7_gmu_load_fw / gen7_gmu_version_info do: the size-0 PREALLOC/PERSIST
blocks outside ITCM/DTCM get zeroed memory of ours mapped at their GMU addresses through context 1
(ICACHE 0x4000, 0x100000, 0x200000, 0x300000; 0x60000000, 0x60001000), then TLBIASID+sync; data
blocks go into ITCM (0x0) / DTCM (0x10004000) through the GMU's registers (CM3 held in reset), each
read back word by word, or are copied into that memory (the code at 0x4000); finally the version
words at DTCM +0xff8 (kgsl wants core >= 0x40000000). TCM contents are not restored; the memory
is freed at the end.

